          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-12 20:08:03.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: reload LNet on all nodes in conf-sanity 73c",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: reload LNet on all nodes in conf-sanity 73c\n\nconf-sanity test_73c runs \"lnetctl net add\" 36 times on ost1. In\nCI most of them take 17-60 s, and the test 15-19 minutes. Its\nfirst cleanup unloads the modules only on the client that runs\nthe test (LOAD_MODULES_REMOTE is false in CI), so ost1 keeps the\nLNet that test_73b used. That has about 100 configured peers for\nthe unreachable NIDs that 73b writes into mgsnode and failnode.\nDiscovery of those peers holds the socklnd connd threads in\nconnect(), and each net add waits for a Push in flight to time\nout (fixed in LNet under LU-21201).\n\nUnload the modules on every node at the start of the test, as the\ntest's stack_trap cleanup already does at its end. ost1 then\nstarts from a fresh LNet. The test still configures 36 nets on\nost1 and mounts the servers, so its coverage does not change.\n\nOn a 2-node VM cluster, 73b then 73c with LOAD_MODULES_REMOTE=false\nas in CI: 73c took 1146 s before and 171 s after.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=73\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7a267dfbddee3cac3fe3b7e12fe1adaadcebdde2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
